dalia-learning-resource:9de0893b-39b5-4fc4-b8c7-af70fa01b328 a ec:EducationalResource ;
    dcterms:description "What is the IPFS \"IPFS (InterPlanetary File System) is a distributed system for storing and accessing files, websites, applications, and data.\" How does the IPFS support FAIR Data Workflows? Findable: In the IPFS each data block has a unique content identifier (CID). These content identifiers can easily included in existing data catalogues in order to make the data findable Accessible: IPFS data can be accessed from anywhere and anytime without authentication or authorization. This makes it a truly open network. Interoperable: Python libraries, such es xArray can access data directly access data in the IPFS. This makes it easy to interoperate IPFS data within existing work flows. Reproducible: Data within the IPFS is immutable. This ensures the reproducibility of workflows over a long time period." ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-3/eng> ;
    dcterms:license mo:ProprietaryLicense ;
    dcterms:title "Incubator IPFS Pinning Tutorial" ;
    ns1:authorUnordered [ a schema:Organization ;
            schema:name "NFDI4Earth" ] ;
    mo:hasCommunity dalia-community:2156f39a-e2f4-4386-893c-4ecf4e8a6630 ;
