dalia-learning-resource:af9fe017-fe6b-4ff4-bfcf-61d33ddf7bbc a ec:EducationalResource ;
    dcterms:description """"Who owns my data? On our way to open data - Nagoya and beyond!" - under this workshop titel, Dr. Amber Hartman Scholz presents the facts of the Nagoya Protocol at the SFE2 GfÖ EEF Joint Meeting, the International Conference on Ecological Sciences 2022. She is Head of Science Policy Department and Deputy to the Director at the Leibniz Institute DSMZ, the German Collection of Microorganims and Cell Cultures, and an expert in science policy, microbiology and genomics. The DSMZ is one of the about 50 partner institutions of NFDI4Biodiversity.
In this workshop, she presents the current debate on whether digital sequence information (DSI) is subject to the Nagoya Protocol and why the answer to this question could have serious implications on global research.

More information about NFDI4Biodiversity can be found on our website (www.nfdi4biodiversity.org) and on Twitter (@NFDI4Biodiv).""" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-3/eng> ;
    dcterms:license <http://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-3.0> ;
    dcterms:title "\"Who owns my data?\" - Workshop by Dr. Amber Hartman Scholz at the SFE2 GfÖ EEF Joint Meeting 2022" ;
    ns1:authorUnordered [ a schema:Organization ;
            schema:name "NFDI4Biodiversity" ] ;
