dalia-learning-resource:fc6bc316-8fad-43b3-afa9-9845372273f9 a ec:EducationalResource ;
    dcterms:description """GHGA aims to address the needs for establishing a national genome archive for human genome data while tackling challenges in data access, sharing, and privacy. GHGA aims provide a national infrastructure for secure and safe storage, access management, dissemination, and analysis of human omics data under a coherent ethical-legal framework. 

The core objectives of GHGA are as follows:

To build a platform for long-term FAIR data archival of human omics data that are being generated at the major omics centers in Germany
Provide Controlled access management and community-centric data sharing platforms
Provide an ethico-legal and data use framework for data sharing, protection and analysis
Enable distributed analytics to democratize data processing and research reuse
Establish strong interfaces with international genome initiatives and become THE german node in the new Federated EGA""" ;
    dcterms:format "PDF" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-3/eng> ;
    dcterms:license <http://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0> ;
    dcterms:title "EATRIS Summer School in Precision Medicine - German Human Genome-Phenome Archive" ;
    ns1:authorUnordered [ a schema:Person ;
